(2125606, 287177, 11960, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>First off, I think this picture is really great. It fits the challenge well, and is pleasing to the eye. <br/> <br/>The two different shades of yellow add intrest and give a balanced feel to the image. I gives me a calm, soothing feeling. This is added to by the lines created by the vase and the petals. I like the way the bottom of the petals seem to become a continuation of the side of the vase, further unifing the elements of this photo.<br/> <br/>The lighting here is good. There doesn''t seem to be any problems with over/underexposure, and again the colors are great. <br/> <br/>The only nitpick I can find with this shot is perhaps the cropping on the bottom. I would have liked to have seen the vase extend all of the way into the corner. I know that''s not kosher photography, but just a thought.<br/> <br/>This is a great shot. Well done!<br/> <br/>Trey</td>', '*Critique Club* First off, I think this picture is really great. It fits the challenge well, and is pleasing to the eye.  The two different shades of yellow add intrest and give a balanced feel to the image. I gives me a calm, soothing feeling. This is added to by the lines created by the vase and the petals. I like the way the bottom of the petals seem to become a continuation of the side of the vase, further unifing the elements of this photo. The lighting here is good. There doesn''t seem to be any problems with over/underexposure, and again the colors are great.  The only nitpick I can find with this shot is perhaps the cropping on the bottom. I would have liked to have seen the vase extend all of the way into the corner. I know that''s not kosher photography, but just a thought. This is a great shot. Well done! Trey', '2006-02-06 00:26:57.000000', NULL, 0),
