(2141703, 287101, 41802, '<td valign="top">* Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Winter Pond" is nice fit in the Off Center category.   I think this would have fit well into a nature category as well.  This strikes me as a nice, quite, calm piece.  <br/> <br/>Technically the shot looks OK.  The grass appears to be a little too green, almost as if the contrast was turned up too high.   I really do like that you left surrounding objects in to show the depth of field.  I feel as thought I am just sitting and looking out on the water, and very cold while I am doing so.  I think the illusion of cold <br/>is coming from the crisp color of the water, plus the snow (more then likely it wasn''t an illusion for you).  I would probably say if the subject had a little more interest it would have grabbed the voters .  Keep up the good work.</td>', '* Critique Club* "Winter Pond" is nice fit in the Off Center category.   I think this would have fit well into a nature category as well.  This strikes me as a nice, quite, calm piece.   Technically the shot looks OK.  The grass appears to be a little too green, almost as if the contrast was turned up too high.   I really do like that you left surrounding objects in to show the depth of field.  I feel as thought I am just sitting and looking out on the water, and very cold while I am doing so.  I think the illusion of cold is coming from the crisp color of the water, plus the snow (more then likely it wasn''t an illusion for you).  I would probably say if the subject had a little more interest it would have grabbed the voters .  Keep up the good work.', '2006-02-11 00:02:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2141798, 287909, 41802, '<td valign="top">* Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"My Best Side" defiantly meets the Off Centered Challenge.  The title is a great element to set the mood of your piece. <br/> <br/>The shot itself is very nicely taken.  I really do love the feel and composition. The  second bird makes it obvious who the odd man out is.  I think you left enough in the background to keep it interesting but still aloud the subject to remain the focus without some sort of distraction.  The only thing I could possibly see changing is leaving the feet/legs in the shot.  What I find really amazing is their is not bird poo on the railing the birds are sitting on. Overall this is really a great shot.</td>', '* Critique Club* "My Best Side" defiantly meets the Off Centered Challenge.  The title is a great element to set the mood of your piece.  The shot itself is very nicely taken.  I really do love the feel and composition. The  second bird makes it obvious who the odd man out is.  I think you left enough in the background to keep it interesting but still aloud the subject to remain the focus without some sort of distraction.  The only thing I could possibly see changing is leaving the feet/legs in the shot.  What I find really amazing is their is not bird poo on the railing the birds are sitting on. Overall this is really a great shot.', '2006-02-11 00:26:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142224, 287950, 12611, '<td valign="top">Great shot.</td>', 'Great shot.', '2006-02-11 08:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142338, 287233, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club.</b> <br/> <br/>A great photo, well deserving of a ribbon. The composition works very well, especially putting the subject off-center. The reflection is colorful and abstract, and certainly interesting but not really powerful enough to stand on its own. Embedding it in bland (although far from being devoid of interest) and concrete setting makes it stand out. The combination is far greater than its parts. Very well done. Congratuations!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.  A great photo, well deserving of a ribbon. The composition works very well, especially putting the subject off-center. The reflection is colorful and abstract, and certainly interesting but not really powerful enough to stand on its own. Embedding it in bland (although far from being devoid of interest) and concrete setting makes it stand out. The combination is far greater than its parts. Very well done. Congratuations!', '2006-02-11 10:34:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142357, 286796, 42638, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Very good composition here Kita. I think the comment concerning it looking centered is due to the fact that his upper body begins in the center, although his head is off center, it may have been tricky for some to see the difference. The lighting is pretty good, a bit too much on his neck and cheek. I like the color of his shirt and yes, even with wrinkles. That is what many busy boys end up in, It seems to really add to his expression. His arm serves as a nice line leading the viewers eye to his wonderful expression. You''ve really captured a beautiful expression here. Looks like he is really focusing on what he wants to do next and maybe a little frustration and boredom too. I don''t see it being out of focus as one commenter mentioned, his face has a good softness about it that really brings out his character. Overall, I think you did a fine job at this profile picture. There is good use of space and rule of thirds. The positioning may not have worked well in this challenge but it is appealing and technically right on track.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Very good composition here Kita. I think the comment concerning it looking centered is due to the fact that his upper body begins in the center, although his head is off center, it may have been tricky for some to see the difference. The lighting is pretty good, a bit too much on his neck and cheek. I like the color of his shirt and yes, even with wrinkles. That is what many busy boys end up in, It seems to really add to his expression. His arm serves as a nice line leading the viewers eye to his wonderful expression. You''ve really captured a beautiful expression here. Looks like he is really focusing on what he wants to do next and maybe a little frustration and boredom too. I don''t see it being out of focus as one commenter mentioned, his face has a good softness about it that really brings out his character. Overall, I think you did a fine job at this profile picture. There is good use of space and rule of thirds. The positioning may not have worked well in this challenge but it is appealing and technically right on track. ', '2006-02-11 10:48:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142378, 285429, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club.</b> <br/> <br/>I like the simplicity of this photo. The lights bring out the texture of the wall and form an interesting shape. But it is lacking a good focal point; the light switch is too low in the frame to be one, leaving the rather vague shape cast by the middle light, which is in a good place but just isn''t very interesting.<br/> <br/>It also isn''t clear to me what message this photo is trying to convey. Red tends to evoke passion and energy, but the vertical line of the wires with the sinuous swath of illumination behind it suggest something closer to harmony or confidence. Stringing the lights diagonally would better suit the red color, or a blue color would better suit the vertical lights.<br/> <br/>But on the positive side, the technical aspects of this photo (focus, exposure, etc.) are great. And the negative space on the right which is dark but not completely black works very well.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.  I like the simplicity of this photo. The lights bring out the texture of the wall and form an interesting shape. But it is lacking a good focal point; the light switch is too low in the frame to be one, leaving the rather vague shape cast by the middle light, which is in a good place but just isn''t very interesting. It also isn''t clear to me what message this photo is trying to convey. Red tends to evoke passion and energy, but the vertical line of the wires with the sinuous swath of illumination behind it suggest something closer to harmony or confidence. Stringing the lights diagonally would better suit the red color, or a blue color would better suit the vertical lights. But on the positive side, the technical aspects of this photo (focus, exposure, etc.) are great. And the negative space on the right which is dark but not completely black works very well.', '2006-02-11 11:13:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142461, 287848, 5112, '<td valign="top">Beautiful!  You''re good at these.  I love it when borders are used to enhance the image.</td>', 'Beautiful!  You''re good at these.  I love it when borders are used to enhance the image.', '2006-02-11 11:46:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142495, 287921, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I see you have had some good comments through your Forum dialog, and I''m delighted to have the chance to add to them through the Critique Club as I have just drawn your image out of the queue.<br/> <br/>I think your Photorapher''s Comment of "Last Minute Submission" may be the key to your rather low score on this bright image.  It is rather difficult to tell just what the focal point of this image is and that always confuses the voters.  Because you have several very white areas in your image, they tend to draw one''s attention, but I think you want the viewer to look at the upper left corner where the stylized heart is.<br/> <br/>I suspect that if you had had just a bit more time to work with this concept, and perhaps bracketed your shots, you might have come up with a composition that the viewers could appreciate a bit more.  Bracketing might also subdue the very strong red - or the addition of just a touch of blue would also calm the color down a bit.<br/> <br/>All in all, I think you just needed a bit more time with this one, and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC.  Your other work tells me you have a good eye.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  I see you have had some good comments through your Forum dialog, and I''m delighted to have the chance to add to them through the Critique Club as I have just drawn your image out of the queue. I think your Photorapher''s Comment of "Last Minute Submission" may be the key to your rather low score on this bright image.  It is rather difficult to tell just what the focal point of this image is and that always confuses the voters.  Because you have several very white areas in your image, they tend to draw one''s attention, but I think you want the viewer to look at the upper left corner where the stylized heart is. I suspect that if you had had just a bit more time to work with this concept, and perhaps bracketed your shots, you might have come up with a composition that the viewers could appreciate a bit more.  Bracketing might also subdue the very strong red - or the addition of just a touch of blue would also calm the color down a bit. All in all, I think you just needed a bit more time with this one, and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC.  Your other work tells me you have a good eye.', '2006-02-11 12:05:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142558, 287921, 32133, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sfalice:</b></div><hr/><i> <b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>I see you have had some good comments through your Forum dialog, and I''m delighted to have the chance to add to them through the Critique Club as I have just drawn your image out of the queue.<br/> <br/>I think your Photorapher''s Comment of "Last Minute Submission" may be the key to your rather low score on this bright image.  It is rather difficult to tell just what the focal point of this image is and that always confuses the voters.  Because you have several very white areas in your image, they tend to draw one''s attention, but I think you want the viewer to look at the upper left corner where the stylized heart is.<br/> <br/>I suspect that if you had had just a bit more time to work with this concept, and perhaps bracketed your shots, you might have come up with a composition that the viewers could appreciate a bit more.  Bracketing might also subdue the very strong red - or the addition of just a touch of blue would also calm the color down a bit.<br/> <br/>All in all, I think you just needed a bit more time with this one, and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC.  Your other work tells me you have a good eye. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for all your thoughtful comments.  I''ll be working on this one some more because I actually really love it.</td>', 'Originally posted by sfalice: Greetings from the Critique Club  I see you have had some good comments through your Forum dialog, and I''m delighted to have the chance to add to them through the Critique Club as I have just drawn your image out of the queue. I think your Photorapher''s Comment of "Last Minute Submission" may be the key to your rather low score on this bright image.  It is rather difficult to tell just what the focal point of this image is and that always confuses the voters.  Because you have several very white areas in your image, they tend to draw one''s attention, but I think you want the viewer to look at the upper left corner where the stylized heart is. I suspect that if you had had just a bit more time to work with this concept, and perhaps bracketed your shots, you might have come up with a composition that the viewers could appreciate a bit more.  Bracketing might also subdue the very strong red - or the addition of just a touch of blue would also calm the color down a bit. All in all, I think you just needed a bit more time with this one, and I''ll look forward to seeing more of your work on DPC.  Your other work tells me you have a good eye.   Thanks for all your thoughtful comments.  I''ll be working on this one some more because I actually really love it.', '2006-02-11 12:47:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142560, 287517, 42638, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Very interesting picture. Good texture and lighting. The shadows seem to accentuate the texture well, good position. The one thing that really bothers me about this is the background. Other than the obvious brighter shine directly behind the statue, my eyes seem to go straight for that vase in the middle. I think with the light reflecting on the pillar directly behind the statue and then to the left onto the vase and continues to the shade, its very distracting from your subject. Its almost a leading line away from your subject. With advanced editing, I believe you can select all but the statue and darken it to that there is less competition. I like the similar color hues but it doesn''t help with this background set up. I don''t mean to sound so negative because I really like your subject. With a little bit more editing, I think it would really power up this picture.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Very interesting picture. Good texture and lighting. The shadows seem to accentuate the texture well, good position. The one thing that really bothers me about this is the background. Other than the obvious brighter shine directly behind the statue, my eyes seem to go straight for that vase in the middle. I think with the light reflecting on the pillar directly behind the statue and then to the left onto the vase and continues to the shade, its very distracting from your subject. Its almost a leading line away from your subject. With advanced editing, I believe you can select all but the statue and darken it to that there is less competition. I like the similar color hues but it doesn''t help with this background set up. I don''t mean to sound so negative because I really like your subject. With a little bit more editing, I think it would really power up this picture.', '2006-02-11 12:51:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2142782, 287994, 11078, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a beautiful clear crisp image <br/>You really deserve your Ribbon well done!</td>', 'Congratulations on a beautiful clear crisp image You really deserve your Ribbon well done!', '2006-02-11 14:55:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2143288, 288049, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 4.  In my opinion it was off-centered ''enough'' to adequately meet the Challenge, but the overall composition and elements didn''t really emphasize the placement nor the subject or ''story'' enough.  As best I can recall, I first saw it and accepted it as ''met the Challenge'', then moved on to what it was, the quality and then the concept/story/title.  As far as I knew/know, ''snake eye(s)'' is 1 on the die/dice - so when looking at this, whilst I thought the placement of the one ''pip'' (just learned through commenting on this that''s the term for the ''dot'') was odd, but honestly didn''t study it long enough to see manipulation, visual effect, etc.  I think the concept is quite good but would need to be ''captured'' in a very strong way, without any distractions.  The surface the die is on blends from black to brown and also has a few minor ''blemishes''.  The blank white area on the die was quite dominant, especially over the somewhat weak reflection - which if that were stronger, would also have likely helped this in my opinion.  Perhaps also a more finely tuned crop, especially at the top to give the die <i>and</i> reflection a better position within the frame, and possibly a nudge rotation for more symmetry, may have also helped make this a stronger image - again, just my opinion.  Perhaps using just the ''natural 1 pip'' and cloning it out on the real and leaving it on the reflection - but then I realize perhaps you did it this way as .. the pip is also off-centered.  If so, that was lost on me during voting due to ''attention time''.</td>', 'I gave this a 4.  In my opinion it was off-centered ''enough'' to adequately meet the Challenge, but the overall composition and elements didn''t really emphasize the placement nor the subject or ''story'' enough.  As best I can recall, I first saw it and accepted it as ''met the Challenge'', then moved on to what it was, the quality and then the concept/story/title.  As far as I knew/know, ''snake eye(s)'' is 1 on the die/dice - so when looking at this, whilst I thought the placement of the one ''pip'' (just learned through commenting on this that''s the term for the ''dot'') was odd, but honestly didn''t study it long enough to see manipulation, visual effect, etc.  I think the concept is quite good but would need to be ''captured'' in a very strong way, without any distractions.  The surface the die is on blends from black to brown and also has a few minor ''blemishes''.  The blank white area on the die was quite dominant, especially over the somewhat weak reflection - which if that were stronger, would also have likely helped this in my opinion.  Perhaps also a more finely tuned crop, especially at the top to give the die and reflection a better position within the frame, and possibly a nudge rotation for more symmetry, may have also helped make this a stronger image - again, just my opinion.  Perhaps using just the ''natural 1 pip'' and cloning it out on the real and leaving it on the reflection - but then I realize perhaps you did it this way as .. the pip is also off-centered.  If so, that was lost on me during voting due to ''attention time''.', '2006-02-11 19:46:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2144467, 287999, 45764, '<td valign="top">Very nice... I love the colors and the lighting.</td>', 'Very nice... I love the colors and the lighting.', '2006-02-12 13:32:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2144476, 287999, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Daisy" is a prefect fit into the Off Center challenge.  Just from the very first glance at this shot it looks like a very nice attractive shot. I think a lot of time people glance through the thumbnails to see which shots they want to vote on and this one is bound to grab their attention.  <br/> <br/>The image its self is very striking, I think you used the prefect color combination to have a natural look but enough contrast to bring out the subject.  I think the glow on the flower makes this piece, but that is my opinion.  I also like how it feels softer because of the glow.  The composition and lighting are excellent in my opinion as well as the diffusion.  I really thought it would place higher.  Keep up the excellent work.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Daisy" is a prefect fit into the Off Center challenge.  Just from the very first glance at this shot it looks like a very nice attractive shot. I think a lot of time people glance through the thumbnails to see which shots they want to vote on and this one is bound to grab their attention.   The image its self is very striking, I think you used the prefect color combination to have a natural look but enough contrast to bring out the subject.  I think the glow on the flower makes this piece, but that is my opinion.  I also like how it feels softer because of the glow.  The composition and lighting are excellent in my opinion as well as the diffusion.  I really thought it would place higher.  Keep up the excellent work.', '2006-02-12 13:38:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2144498, 288054, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Painful grip" seems like a  pretty well centered shot. Maybe you were referring to off center because the subject is upside down, I could see that.  I think the full frame seeming pretty centered might be why the score was not higher. <br/> <br/>The shot itself is amazing in its timing.  I really like the motion that you captured with the slow blur/glow around the movement of the legs.   The composition is great. Even the composition really isn''t effected by the lady in the background watching because it is such a strong subject.  Also good use of diffusion to soften the edges and allow to focus to remain on the subject.   This really is an awesome action shot.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Painful grip" seems like a  pretty well centered shot. Maybe you were referring to off center because the subject is upside down, I could see that.  I think the full frame seeming pretty centered might be why the score was not higher.  The shot itself is amazing in its timing.  I really like the motion that you captured with the slow blur/glow around the movement of the legs.   The composition is great. Even the composition really isn''t effected by the lady in the background watching because it is such a strong subject.  Also good use of diffusion to soften the edges and allow to focus to remain on the subject.   This really is an awesome action shot.', '2006-02-12 14:03:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2144547, 287589, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Glow" is a very striking piece, defiantly grabbed my attention.  This meets the off center challenge, I really like how it is off centered yet you mange to leave the image balanced.   <br/> <br/>The glow is absolutely amazing, the coloring is so strong.  This really looks like a shot for a movie cover, like Hunt for Red October.  The sun look unreal.  I really like the crop and how you used the length to fit the boat.   The composition is excellent, it really feels like a complete shot.  <br/> <br/>I think the off center challenge is one were people really do have a specific idea in their minds and are really looking for an off balance shot, that''s the only think I can really see as to way your shot did not place higher.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Glow" is a very striking piece, defiantly grabbed my attention.  This meets the off center challenge, I really like how it is off centered yet you mange to leave the image balanced.    The glow is absolutely amazing, the coloring is so strong.  This really looks like a shot for a movie cover, like Hunt for Red October.  The sun look unreal.  I really like the crop and how you used the length to fit the boat.   The composition is excellent, it really feels like a complete shot.   I think the off center challenge is one were people really do have a specific idea in their minds and are really looking for an off balance shot, that''s the only think I can really see as to way your shot did not place higher.', '2006-02-12 14:34:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2144594, 287754, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Right of Center (for a while)" fits into the Off Center challenge. At first glance I really do like this, especially because it is something different to see.   Also I think creativity for the title was a very excellent element of this piece, in the challenge.  <br/> <br/>The composition of this image is very lovely.  There is a very nice overall feel to the shot.  Also I like that you were able to include the fountain and give the shot some movement. One thing that is a little unsettling is there seems to be a tilt from the bottom left side, I think it wouldn''t be so obvious if it were for the house.  Since the viewer is drawn to the house they start to look at the top and wonder if the shot is uneven.  It is a small enough title not to make the image completely unusable, but probably noticeable.  Good work. <br/></td>', '*Critique Club* "Right of Center (for a while)" fits into the Off Center challenge. At first glance I really do like this, especially because it is something different to see.   Also I think creativity for the title was a very excellent element of this piece, in the challenge.   The composition of this image is very lovely.  There is a very nice overall feel to the shot.  Also I like that you were able to include the fountain and give the shot some movement. One thing that is a little unsettling is there seems to be a tilt from the bottom left side, I think it wouldn''t be so obvious if it were for the house.  Since the viewer is drawn to the house they start to look at the top and wonder if the shot is uneven.  It is a small enough title not to make the image completely unusable, but probably noticeable.  Good work. ', '2006-02-12 15:00:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2145111, 286846, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Interesting shapes ... and interesting location.  I would never have guess.<br/> <br/>Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Yes you can say it is off centred, and in that way it works, but really it does not seem to take into account the rule of thirds, which could have helped make this shot, all that would really take is a few more goes at cropping the image.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>You have met the challenge with gusto!<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This is one of those times I feel like saying black and white overkill, but I don''t know what colours there actually are, and how they could have enhanced the shot.  <br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>It was a solid effort, I think that taking a look at how you have cropped may have helped to create better leading lines, and really is thing an image that should be b&amp;w????<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good shot, it scored well and is nicely now on the front page of your portfolio.  Meets the challenge, and to me that is important ...especially with an out of the box idea!!!<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Interesting shapes ... and interesting location.  I would never have guess. Interesting to do a critique on your image but it is difficult if you don''t give us any information in your photographers comments.  When we do a critique, we go past just the photographic result, that''s what voters comments do.  The critique looks at what you were trying to achieve, how you wanted it to look and what issues you had in getting the image captured and ready for voting. Composition: Yes you can say it is off centred, and in that way it works, but really it does not seem to take into account the rule of thirds, which could have helped make this shot, all that would really take is a few more goes at cropping the image. Subject: You have met the challenge with gusto! Technical (Colour and light): This is one of those times I feel like saying black and white overkill, but I don''t know what colours there actually are, and how they could have enhanced the shot.   To grow its vote?: It was a solid effort, I think that taking a look at how you have cropped may have helped to create better leading lines, and really is thing an image that should be b&w???? Summary: Good shot, it scored well and is nicely now on the front page of your portfolio.  Meets the challenge, and to me that is important ...especially with an out of the box idea!!! If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-02-12 19:23:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2145127, 286785, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Lovely colours, with an interesting perspective.  What a take on the challenge.  Did you happen upon this or did you set it up ... <br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Well composed with  great use of DOF ... the details of the wood is fantastic ... and it looks like you can touch it.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Defiantely meets my idea of a off centred.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Nature provides us with fantastic lighting ... and you have made the most of this.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>You are in a tough challenge here, and I think this shot did really well, to grow .. perhaps look at the cropping, but don''t panic is really quite unreal.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>The comments you have received reflect the different emotions and feelings that have been evoked from this shot .. great work.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Lovely colours, with an interesting perspective.  What a take on the challenge.  Did you happen upon this or did you set it up ...  Composition: Well composed with  great use of DOF ... the details of the wood is fantastic ... and it looks like you can touch it. Subject: Defiantely meets my idea of a off centred. Technical (Colour and light): Nature provides us with fantastic lighting ... and you have made the most of this. To grow its vote?: You are in a tough challenge here, and I think this shot did really well, to grow .. perhaps look at the cropping, but don''t panic is really quite unreal. Summary: The comments you have received reflect the different emotions and feelings that have been evoked from this shot .. great work. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-02-12 19:29:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2145138, 287108, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>The lushness is great, the first impression is lovely.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>"great shot" quote from a commentor ... and it is.  I think that the ways I can see this improving include a different crop, perhaps working the deer towards the thirds line.  The fllen tree works the horizontal thirds well.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Defiantely meets off centred and gives the impression of being left behind.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>This shot is a little dark, but nature has provided and done ok with the lighting. I think adding a little brightness may have assisted, but it also may have killed it, so it works leave it!<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>Top 100 .. I think that is good.  It is a solid shot, with some good emotions evoked.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Well done, I think that you have some fantastic ideas in your portfolio and come from left field alot ... keep doing it.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: The lushness is great, the first impression is lovely. Composition: "great shot" quote from a commentor ... and it is.  I think that the ways I can see this improving include a different crop, perhaps working the deer towards the thirds line.  The fllen tree works the horizontal thirds well. Subject: Defiantely meets off centred and gives the impression of being left behind. Technical (Colour and light): This shot is a little dark, but nature has provided and done ok with the lighting. I think adding a little brightness may have assisted, but it also may have killed it, so it works leave it! To grow its vote?: Top 100 .. I think that is good.  It is a solid shot, with some good emotions evoked. Summary: Well done, I think that you have some fantastic ideas in your portfolio and come from left field alot ... keep doing it. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-02-12 19:37:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2145180, 285772, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Nice, good focus, great portrait work.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Good composition, it doesn''t rellay play too heavy of the notice you used for the title, and that may have confused the voters ... who are often confused :)<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Defiantely meets off centred, both for the bloke and the signage.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>I like the lighting here, would have liked to know what you actually used ... but probably daylight in the majority with a fill flash ... oh well :)<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>You have found an interesting character - again.  It is nicely off centred, I don''t know why it did not do better, the grittiness of the colours and the reality of the picture may have counted against it this time.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I like this shot, it is good for the portfolio, even if not the highest scoring.  But this game ain''t only about ribbons really.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Nice, good focus, great portrait work. Composition: Good composition, it doesn''t rellay play too heavy of the notice you used for the title, and that may have confused the voters ... who are often confused :) Subject: Defiantely meets off centred, both for the bloke and the signage. Technical (Colour and light): I like the lighting here, would have liked to know what you actually used ... but probably daylight in the majority with a fill flash ... oh well :) To grow its vote?: You have found an interesting character - again.  It is nicely off centred, I don''t know why it did not do better, the grittiness of the colours and the reality of the picture may have counted against it this time. Summary: I like this shot, it is good for the portfolio, even if not the highest scoring.  But this game ain''t only about ribbons really. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-02-12 20:00:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2145195, 287996, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Not often I get to critique something I commented on. :)<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I thought this was well composed with good use of DOF.<br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Meets the challenge and is very off centred.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Good lighting, good dof, maybe the cropping could have improved the shot and taken it from over average to better.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>I think that perhaps the cropping may have been the issue for some ... having the crop slightly wider on the left (looking at the screen) ... may have given a little more proportion.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Great shot ... I like your model and use of her here.  <br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari<br/>=====</td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Not often I get to critique something I commented on. :) Composition: I thought this was well composed with good use of DOF. Subject: Meets the challenge and is very off centred. Technical (Colour and light): Good lighting, good dof, maybe the cropping could have improved the shot and taken it from over average to better. To grow its vote?: I think that perhaps the cropping may have been the issue for some ... having the crop slightly wider on the left (looking at the screen) ... may have given a little more proportion. Summary: Great shot ... I like your model and use of her here.   If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari=====', '2006-02-12 20:06:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2145230, 287835, 43434, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Interesting shot, but lacks focus.  I checked your portfolio .. all of your higher scoring shots have that focus point.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>It pays to rotate .. off centred does not actually mean crooked.  You can tell this by the angle that the lamppost is on.  <br/> <br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>This is a good night time shot ... one i dream of being able to achieve one day myself.  it defiantely meets the challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Well lit amd well done for an evening shoot.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>There needs to be a true focus point, fine details such as straightening need attention for all shots.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Good addition to the portfolio.  You have also recieved some valuable comments from voters which you should note.<br/> <br/>If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Kari<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-02-12 20:27:07.</i></td>', '::: Critique Club :::  Hi, my name is Kari and from the critique club. First Impression - the most important one: Interesting shot, but lacks focus.  I checked your portfolio .. all of your higher scoring shots have that focus point. Composition: It pays to rotate .. off centred does not actually mean crooked.  You can tell this by the angle that the lamppost is on.   Subject: This is a good night time shot ... one i dream of being able to achieve one day myself.  it defiantely meets the challenge. Technical (Colour and light): Well lit amd well done for an evening shoot. To grow its vote?: There needs to be a true focus point, fine details such as straightening need attention for all shots. Summary: Good addition to the portfolio.  You have also recieved some valuable comments from voters which you should note. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via the PM system. Cheers Kari', '2006-02-12 20:25:32.000000', '2006-02-12 20:27:07.000000', 0),
